# (Empty for now.) The listings/ directory used to live here so the
# auto-generated per-question Turtle fragments stayed out of git.
# That broke Overleaf, which has no way to run build-listings.sh
# itself, so the per-paper subsections couldn't \lstinputlisting any
# of the fragments and the compile failed.
#
# Decision (2026-04-28): commit listings/ to keep Overleaf compiles
# working. Do NOT hand-edit files under listings/ -- they are
# regenerated from the canonical artifacts/kg/papers/<paper-id>.ttl
# by artifacts/kg/build-listings.sh and overwritten on every run.
# Hand edits will be silently lost.
#
# A future refactor will separate the data-generation work from the
# paper repo into a sibling repo, restoring "auto-generated content
# stays out of source" while keeping Overleaf compileable. Until
# then, listings/ stays tracked and round-trip + build-listings stay
# part of the workflow before each push that touches the catalogue.
